WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.440
This is called a searched case expression Each WHEN
contains a complete

00:00:05.466 --> 00:00:10.635
Boolean condition That makes searched case useful
for ranges null checks and

00:00:10.661 --> 00:00:16.692
compound rules In this example we classify billing
amounts Missing

00:00:16.718 --> 00:00:21.743
amounts become Unknown Amounts greater than or equal
to ten thousand become

00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:26.653
High Value Amounts greater than or equal to five
thousand become Standard

00:00:27.568 --> 00:00:32.783
Everything else becomes Low Value We have the full
SQL in the

00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:37.294
runnable code cell Click Run in the browser and
compare the original

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.008
bill amount with the new billing tier You can also
click Copy

00:00:42.034 --> 00:00:46.790
and run the same query in pgAdmin When reading this
query focus

00:00:46.816 --> 00:00:51.520
on the decision order rather than the punctuation
SQL is simply checking

00:00:51.546 --> 00:00:54.252
each rule from top to bottom and using the first
rule that

00:00:54.265 --> 00:00:54.819
matches
